      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/bruington_virginia",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Captain Whittaker Campbell established the Brewington plantation in the mid‑18th century, operating a subsistence farm that listed 5–10 enslaved tithables in 1782‑86.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/bruington_virginia",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Bruington’s proximity to the Rappahannock River creates fertile soils and wetlands that support deer, turkey, and diverse bird species.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4,
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
